{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"mopey-living-viper","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Revise the T10 (overlay-infra) rubric to partition its scope away from the transient de-risking phase, so T10 and T15 cover disjoint phases. There is no runtime cross-criterion suppression by design, so the boundary must live in T10's own rubric text.\n\n## Work\n- Edit src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T10.md: add a scope clause near the top: \"This overlay evaluates the DURABLE infrastructure — the IaC/config that persists. Transient, throwaway experiments used to de-risk a mechanism before committing it — their creation, isolation, and teardown — are out of scope here.\"\n- T10 must NOT name T15 or reference what any other overlay owns.\n- Regenerate docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md so the T10 section reflects the edit.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- The T10 rubric contains the durable-infrastructure scope clause and no reference to T15/other overlays.\n- A plan whose only infra is an explicitly throwaway experiment (created, probed, torn down) no longer draws a T10 prevent_destroy/blast-radius finding for that transient resource (verify via eval fixture).\n- `rebar explain T10` and the regenerated guide show the updated scope clause.","id":"0d5f-6745-16bc-403c","parent_id":"8fc2-0306-a9a0-4864","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Revise T10 rubric: durable-infra scope clause (partition from transient de-risk phase)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1784918869605107001,"uuid":"f4aa4278-41a3-404a-aa3c-146b36f3f8b8"}